//? Title: Frozen Eager Models: Reachable Weights Without Training State
//? Subtitle: A snapshot contains values; the consumer still supplies the inference function
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A deployed predictor should use a fixed set of learned values without carrying optimizer slots
or unused training parameters. We select the parameters reached by an executed output, detach
and copy them, then check that live-model mutations do not change the saved predictor. In this
eager library the artifact is NPZ weights and a contract, not a TensorFlow GraphDef.
)
\toc

> The method

For output f(x;theta), the recorded eager graph reveals which parameter tensors are connected
to that output. inference_parameters asks for VJPs with allow_unused: an undefined gradient
means disconnected; a defined zero gradient still means connected. Thus connectivity is not the
same as sensitivity at a single probe. The exported computation in this example is

$$
f(x)=wx+b,\qquad (w,b)=(2,-1/2),\qquad f((-3,1/2,4))=(-13/2,1/2,15/2).
$$
\alttext(The affine function with slope two and intercept minus one half gives predictions minus six point five, point five and seven point five.)

Selecting values excludes optimizer slots and disconnected parameters. Deep copies prevent
later updates from changing the snapshot. The graph is only the executed branch: a different
input-dependent branch may reach other parameters. This is neither static graph pruning nor
serializing program code; the consumer must retain the same inference function and dtype/shape
contract. Selection costs a backward traversal; storage costs the selected parameter bytes.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/frozen_graph_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/frozen_graph_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/frozen_graph_concept.tikz > build/frozen_graph_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/frozen_graph_concept.svg build/frozen_graph_concept.dvi > build/frozen_graph_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/frozen_graph_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
// result_begin:
// Rendered build/frozen_graph_concept.svg from local TikZ source.
// \image(figures/frozen_graph_concept.svg)
// result_end
\caption(A snapshot contains values; the consumer still supplies the inference function)
\alttext(Executed eager output; f(x)=wx+b Then Reachable parameters; defined VJP, even zero Then Detached deep copies; NPZ + consumer code.)

> Simple examples

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/frozen_graph_prediction.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore store;
 auto w=store.get("w",{},n::init::constant(2)),b=store.get("b",{},n::init::constant(-.5));
 store.get("unused",{8},n::init::ones());
 const auto x=n::tensor({-3,.5,4}),y=x*w+b;
 const auto frozen=n::inference_parameters(store,{y});
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::save_npz("build/frozen_graph_weights.npz",frozen);
 {n::NoGradGuard guard;w.copy_(n::scalar(-100));b.copy_(n::scalar(100));}
 n::ParameterStore serving;serving.load("build/frozen_graph_weights.npz",false);
 const auto prediction=x*serving.at("w")+serving.at("b");
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.lines(x.to_vector<double>(),prediction.to_vector<double>(),"saved predictor")
 .title("Saved weights remain independent of live mutation").x_label("x").y_label("prediction");
 p.size(820,420).save_svg("build/frozen_graph_prediction.svg");
 if(frozen.size()!=2||prediction.to_vector<double>()!=std::vector<double>({-6.5,.5,7.5}))return 1;
 std::print("Store arrays: {}; exported arrays: {}.\n\nPredictions: {}.\n",store.size(),frozen.size(),prediction.to_vector<double>());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Store arrays: 3; exported arrays: 2.

Predictions: [-6.5, 0.5, 7.5].
\image(figures/frozen_graph_prediction.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Only the two connected scalar parameters reconstruct the affine predictions.)
\alttext(Only the two connected scalar parameters reconstruct the affine predictions.)

> Checking the theory

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore store;
 const auto w=store.get("connected_zero",{},n::init::ones());store.get("unused",{},n::init::ones());
 const auto snapshot=n::inference_parameters(store,{w*0});
 if(snapshot.size()!=1||snapshot[0].first!="connected_zero"||snapshot[0].second.requires_grad())return 1;
 std::print("Zero derivative still retains connected parameter: {}.\n\nSnapshot requires_grad: {}.\n",snapshot[0].first,snapshot[0].second.requires_grad());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Zero derivative still retains connected parameter: connected_zero.

Snapshot requires_grad: false.
// result_end


> Conclusion

The selected values reproduce the chosen function and remain independent of live mutation.
Zero gradients do not prove a parameter is unused. Since execution can depend on control flow,
a single eager trace is not a universal inference signature or a portable executable model.

> References

- [TensorFlow: GraphDef constant conversion](https://www.tensorflow.org/api_docs/python/tf/compat/v1/graph_util/convert_variables_to_constants).
- [NumPy NPY format specification](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/generated/numpy.lib.format.html).
